# One line ending everywhere: LF in the repository and in the working tree, on
# every platform. Without this, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true (the
# Git-for-Windows default) writes CRLF into the working tree while the index
# holds LF, and three things break at once:
#
#   - scripts/gen-skill-docs.mjs --check generates LF and compares it against
#     the CRLF file on disk, so check.sh reports every line of
#     agents/skills/envy/*.md as changed while showing two identical lines
#   - files sit permanently "modified" with an empty diff (src-tauri/Cargo.toml
#     did exactly this)
#   - a shell script committed with CRLF is not runnable on Linux
#
# eol=lf rather than plain text=auto: the latter still hands Windows CRLF in the
# working tree, which is where the comparison happens.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so git must never translate or diff them as text.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.jpg binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.zst binary
*.tar.gz binary
